1511444.steps:
1. set 10G interface X16 , zone LAN, wiremode bypass mode, pair interface X17, zone LAN, X17 is also a 10G port;
2. Enable link state propagation;
3. Connect X16 to switch A g0/10, connect X17 to switch b G0/11;
4. Shutdown g0/10 on sw A, observe the state of g0/11 on SW B, the link state of interface X16 ,X17;
5. no shutdown g0/10 on SW A, observe the state of g0/10 and g0/11, the link state of interface X16 ,X17;
6. shutdown g0/11 on SW B, observe the state of g0/10 on SW A, the link state of interface X16 ,X17;
7. no shutdown g0/11 on SW B,observe the state of g0/10 and g0/11, the link state of interface X16 ,X17;

1511444.result:
in step 4, g0/10 change to down, g0/11 change to down, X16 and X17 are "no link";
in step 5, g0/10 change to UP, g0/11 change to UP too, X16 and X17 are link up;
in step 6, g0/11 change to down, g0/10 change to down, X16 and X17 are "no link";
in step 7, g0/11 change to UP, g0/10 change to UP too, X16 and X17 are link up;

1511445.steps:
1. In firewall to configure X2, X3 as bypass wire mode, zone selection is LAN-LAN.
2. Configure RIPv2 (multicast mode) in both router 1 and router 2 and redistribute connected route, check if both router can learn routers from peer.
3. Configure OSPF in both router 1 and router 2 and redistribute connected route, check if both router can establish OSPF neighbor and learn routes properly. &#160;
4. Configure BGP in both router1 and router 2 and redistribute connected route, check if both router can establish BGP neighbor and learn routes properly.
5. Configure EIGRP in both router 1 and router 2 and redistribute connected routes, check if both router can establish EIGRP neighbor and learn routes properly. &#160;
6. Enable IP multicast in both router (command: "ip multicast-routing" in global configuration mode), configure IP PIM dense mode in both router's interface (command: "ip pim dense-mode" under interface configuration mode), check if both router can establish PIM neighbor properly (command: "show ip pim neighbor"). &#160;
7. Repeat step 1~6 with other zone combination: LAN-WAN, DMZ-WAN, LAN-DMZ.&#160;
